                <div class="myth-title">Is it "foundation failure"?</div>
                <span class="myth-hint">Tap to see</span>
              </div>
              <div class="myth-back">
                <p>Rarely. Most of what homeowners call failure is soil movement — the ground moving, not the structure losing its ability to stand. "Failure" is urgency language more than an accurate description.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="myth-card" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Tap to flip for the answer">
            <div class="myth-card-inner">
              <div class="myth-front">
                <div class="myth-title">Is every crack serious?</div>
                <span class="myth-hint">Tap to see</span>
              </div>
              <div class="myth-back">
                <p>No. Many reflect historic movement that already stabilized years ago. What matters is whether it's growing now — not whether it exists.</p>
              </div>
